  data: {
    LLM: "Keep middle-range cards (ranks 5-8). These are rarely high enough to win a trick and rarely low enough to lose an exchange round.\n\nThe 'Hus' Block: If you have a 'Hus' (Rank 11), use it to block exchanges from your right-hand neighbor. This forces them to keep their potentially bad card.\n\nHarlekin Timing: If you are the leader, play the Harlekin to win the trick immediately if you suspect the trick contains zero penalty points. If you play it second, ensure it's on a trick you *don't* want to win, as it will be the lowest card.",
    Player: "Keep middle-range cards (ranks 5-8). These are rarely high enough to win a trick and rarely low enough to lose an exchange round.\n\nThe 'Hus' Block: If you have a 'Hus' (Rank 11), use it to block exchanges from your right-hand neighbor. This forces them to keep their potentially bad card.\n\nHarlekin Timing: If you are the leader, play the Harlekin to win the trick immediately if you suspect the trick contains zero penalty points. If you play it second, ensure it's on a trick you *don't* want to win, as it will be the lowest card.",
    aggressiveness: 0.5,
